                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "knoeipotten"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e70d46f0-0b4b-3fc9-8fd6-d0d1d4ea93e3",
                        "entry_id": "f3f89ad5-6c4d-3645-a467-80e4905da93a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een slordig persoon die veel knoeit en daardoor zijn omgeving vies maakt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c305e7e7-1177-412d-a5fe-33e62f8a3370",
                                "sense_id": "e70d46f0-0b4b-3fc9-8fd6-d0d1d4ea93e3",
                                "text": "Een eggtimer voor wie nog geen ei koken kan en voor knoeipotten een vinyl vloermat of een leren schort."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31bcc788-7877-468c-9289-baa53c6b1ddd",
                                "sense_id": "e70d46f0-0b4b-3fc9-8fd6-d0d1d4ea93e3",
                                "text": "„Het is de plicht van een regisseur om de actualiteit van een stuk te benadrukken”, zegt Johan Simons, artistiek leider van de Münchner Kammerspiele en bij TA regisseur van een gewelddadige Macbeth waarin liters bloed over de de speelvloer spat. Simons: „Een stuk als Macbeth dwingt de actualiteit af. Je moet wel een knoeipot van een regisseur zijn als je geen verbinding legt tussen deze tekst bomvol machtswellust en moordzucht en het nu. Voor mij waren de oorlogsfoto’s van de Canadese fotograaf Jeff Wall een inspiratiebron.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16a0ba21-6fc0-46cf-a8f7-519eee016222",
                                "sense_id": "e70d46f0-0b4b-3fc9-8fd6-d0d1d4ea93e3",
                                "text": "Bepaalde mensen mogen vies worden, anderen niet, omdat ze mee moeten naar de koningin.Ik heb veel mensen vies gemaakt, ik ben een knoeipot."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c44f9db-c7bd-4699-bf4e-86377a1da7b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "f3f89ad5-6c4d-3645-a467-80e4905da93a",
                        "source_sense_id": "e70d46f0-0b4b-3fc9-8fd6-d0d1d4ea93e3",
                        "target_lang_word": "bungler",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bungler",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a94b0344-abf3-3f08-b526-5aff5ac91773",
                                        "entry_id": "556c0c06-8c33-3b77-a4fc-7e42191b7b18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who makes mistakes because of incompetence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71873a14-5708-4d52-9cd7-d51b9d26f797",
                                                "sense_id": "a94b0344-abf3-3f08-b526-5aff5ac91773",
                                                "text": "\"What you mean, comparing me to them botchers and bunglers? There ain't anybody but me in the furniture restoring line.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed7feec9-6714-4207-bebf-cbc9b6cc2146",
                                                "sense_id": "a94b0344-abf3-3f08-b526-5aff5ac91773",
                                                "text": "Noble Prophet of Truth, this has gone on long enough. Make an example of this bungler. The Council demands it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "af30f33a-41bd-46e1-a1d3-59943286826a",
                        "source_entry_id": "f3f89ad5-6c4d-3645-a467-80e4905da93a",
                        "source_sense_id": "e70d46f0-0b4b-3fc9-8fd6-d0d1d4ea93e3",
                        "target_lang_word": "botcher",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "botcher",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "712e9775-731e-3037-9092-b4f9bf8b5e05",
                                        "entry_id": "9bd79c92-7d95-3bf7-8cc0-1633f50bcc4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who mends things, especially such a cobbler or tailor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fda620f-e80f-4434-ab14-364b74ffe579",
                                                "sense_id": "712e9775-731e-3037-9092-b4f9bf8b5e05",
                                                "text": "Two faults, madonna, that drink and good counsel will amend: for give the dry fool drink, then is the fool not dry; bid the dishonest man mend himself: if he mend, he is no longer dishonest; if he cannot, let the botcher mend him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44ab3d59-dfc5-30f5-aa06-6e3b190cb0e3",
                                        "entry_id": "9bd79c92-7d95-3bf7-8cc0-1633f50bcc4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "chairmaker"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05c8d3d8-7b43-30f7-93e9-9212a9a8db28",
                                        "entry_id": "9bd79c92-7d95-3bf7-8cc0-1633f50bcc4c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A clumsy or incompetent worker; a bungler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "919479be-df1a-470d-b5f1-73ee562502bd",
                                                "sense_id": "05c8d3d8-7b43-30f7-93e9-9212a9a8db28",
                                                "text": "Dilettanteism presupposes art as botchwork does handicraft; and the Dilettante holds the same relation to the artist that the botcher does to the craftsman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84d4369-604f-431e-beee-170dad77fde6",
                                                "sense_id": "05c8d3d8-7b43-30f7-93e9-9212a9a8db28",
                                                "text": "\"What you mean, comparing me to them botchers and bunglers? There ain't anybody but me in the furniture restoring line.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
